WEBVTT

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.460
It’s nearly Christmas!

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.970
Café Mew Mew’s Christmas cakes are the best!

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.640
Welcome!

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.600
It’s Christmas, have some cake!

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.410
Give me a tip, okay?

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.910
The Special Christmas Cakes are ready now.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.530
Yes!

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.190
Akasaka-san, this hat is really cute!

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:22.870
Thank you very much.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.700
Well I made them with your happiness in mind.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.840
Oh, they’re hand-made?

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.550
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.920
This is the special Deluxe Bu-Ling A La Mode,
Christmas edition, enough for 5 people.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.210
The Christmas Tart.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.260
O... Ok.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:43.840
Good day.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.800
I’m glad that the café is doing well,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.070
but it’s so busy it makes my head spin.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.640
I don’t even have a chance
to drink my tea.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.150
Why are you drinking then?

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.530
I suppose things will stay busy until Christmas.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.560
Keep up the good work, everyone!

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.490
Yes~

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:06.110
But is it just me who’s going to be wearing
this outfit until Christmas?

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.490
Don’t worry Bu-Ling. Look, here!

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.130
I’ve prepared costumes
for the others too.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.740
Are you kidding me?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.470
Waai!

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.050
Everyone will be wearing the same,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:21.620
Christmas. Christmas. Christmas, right?

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.370
I’m so happy!

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.620
Bu-Ling, do you think it’s ok to wear this?

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.830
Why wouldn’t it be?

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.210
I don’t want to wear this.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.390
I guess it’s OK...

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.760
Wah, it’s snowing!

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.980
Yes, it really is.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.640
Ichigo, don’t you feel cold?

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.990
Eh? I’m fine.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.070
So it’s White Christmas, isn’t it?

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.580
Look, now you won’t feel cold.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.790
A-Aoyama-kun.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.670
Call me Masaya.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.220
Masaya.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.430
Ma... Ma-sa-ya.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:07.690
Right.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.150
Good.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.610
Huh?

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.150
Isn’t this weird?

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.860
I thought I’d turn into..

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.110
...if I kiss someone...

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.500
Ichigo!?

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.000
Ichigo turned into a CAT!?

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.780
<i>No, Aoyama-kun!</i>

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:36.960
That... can’t be true.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.410
<i>Wrong wrong, no nooo!</i>

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.200
<i>I’m not a cat, WRONG, no no no no!!</i>

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.180
She’s a cat... a cat... a ca...

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.690
So, what is wrong, Momomiya-san?

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.610
I’m sorry.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.060
Hey, you were shouting in your sleep, Ichigo!

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.110
Really...

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.280
Lately, you’ve been sleeping
quietly, but...

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.820
I... I have to go then.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.980
To the park again?

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.030
Um, yeah...

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.110
Yes. It would be rude to make him wait.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.660
Go already.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.370
OK then, see you tomorrow!

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.370
See you.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.580
Bye.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.790
It’s Christmas time and it seems they’re doing really well.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.000
What do you think?

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.550
Maybe with the Christmas mood they’ll go all the way!

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:36.110
Well, I doubt it.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.800
Why? They might do, mightn’t they?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.100
Well you know, Ichigo is still a child.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.180
Is she childish?

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.220
Sure, she is!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.100
But she may be an “adult”...

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.480
If she’s not a child then it’s only natural for her to...

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.850
Only natural for her to...?

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.530
Well, naturally of course,
you know, they will...

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.750
Wow, so they’ll make love?!?!

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.300
I want to be happy too.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.340
We promised each other not to say that out loud...

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.230
Sorry I made you wait.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.440
No, I was reading.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.980
Ah, I see.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.600
Aoyama-kun, what are your plans for today?

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.480
Well, I don’t have practice today, so I’ll just
drop by the library and be heading home.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.190
What about you?

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.110
Ah, I’m working in the café.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.700
Ah, that’s how it is.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.290
Aoyama-kun.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.550
What kind of book
are you reading today?

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:51.090
Well, this is about the recycling of trash.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:58.670
Mom and I are trying to sort our trash.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:04:59.680
Oh?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.350
We’ve told our neighbors too.
We’d like to help by recycling.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.940
It’s a difficult thing.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.700
I mean such civil-minded activities
are more difficult than you’d think.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.260
People start out willingly,

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.610
but if they push themselves too hard they can’t keep it up for long.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:22.070
But once you’ve started something
like that, it’s not easy to quit.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.540
You can end up feeling guilty.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.290
And it’s not just trash
that’s the problem.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:33.550
Our lifestyle is sure to kill the Earth eventually.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.970
Everyone knows it, but they just keep on as before.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.510
I don’t think we can stop,

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:44.180
because it seems impossible to give
up the pleasant life we have now.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:47.310
Giving up our modern lifestyle would be so
stressful that society might even collapse.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.690
We shouldn’t push ourselves too hard;

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.820
We should just do what we know
we have to, little by little.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.730
Ah, sorry. I talked for too long...

00:05:58.730 --> 00:05:59.880
I got it!

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:03.280
In other words: if you try too hard, you’ll get tired?

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.290
So you should try your best at a normal pace.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.500
Huh. Am I wrong?

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.130
Ichigo... you know,

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:17.840
You’re a genius sometimes.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.210
Ichigo...

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.270
Yes?

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:25.980
Ichigo, have you heard? They’re going to
put a huge Christmas tree up at Odaiba.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.270
Why don’t we go see it together,
on Christmas Eve?

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.820
Is that... Maybe...

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:46.490
I thought you hadn’t been going on many dates recently.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:50.870
Well, we don’t bother to set a time.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.580
We just meet each other after school.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.060
I don’t even care where we go!!

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.270
Congrats.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.650
Congratulations.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.960
Yeah, congrats!

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:00.900
Enough about him!

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.320
Thanks!

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.270
I’m not congratulating you!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.680
So why are you being all merry?

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.800
Ah right, please...

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:12.200
you can call me in on any other day, but please let me take off on Christmas Eve.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.730
I don’t mind.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.330
Good luck, Ichigo!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.370
Yeah, good luck!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.400
Well I guess it’s ok.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.910
Thank you!

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:27.370
It may be fine with us, but we have to consider that enemies might show up.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.710
How do we know you wouldn’t turn up late again?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.080
Ichigo, are you listening?!

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.380
It’s ok it’s ok,
it’s always worked out so far.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.350
Whatever happened, I...

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:44.770
Hey, what are you doing?

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.340
Acting so strangely...

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.310
Hello, Ichigo, you there!?

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:51.860
Ichigo?

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.410
I...

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.150
I...

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.030
Just now...

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.450
What...

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:16.050
And?

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.580
No, I don’t have the slightest idea what she means.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:20.260
I see.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:38.920
I...

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:43.910
I’ve... been lying to Aoyama-kun.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:46.830
And I got totally used to it.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.960
He’s so kind to me and I’m too dependent...

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:53.030
I’m the worst.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:54.290
Ichigo...

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.790
I AM the worst.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:56.790
Ichigo.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.430
Let’s go Christmas shopping.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.890
Sorry about the inconvenience.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.050
It’s nothing.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.400
So?

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:23.720
Ah...

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.450
Sorry, I...

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.540
Why?

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.960
Why do people give presents?

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.010
They entrust their feelings to a thing.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.540
Because feelings aren’t visible to the eyes.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:45.930
But...

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.440
Each person has their own hopes.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:53.070
What part of your heart do you want to open to him?

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.290
I...

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:01.410
In other words, you can’t even see it yourself, in your own heart.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.110
In that case...

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:06.370
you need something to reflect it.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.610
Reflect?

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:08.530
Yes.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:14.050
So the present is something for you as well.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.440
These are the “Tears for Christmas”.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:36.520
“Tears for Christmas”...

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:42.110
Yes. Kurisumasu no namida.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.190
Umm... Thanks a lot.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:50.940
Ichigo...

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:51.330
Yes!

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:57.330
You can give me the money back
when you get otoshidama.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:58.010
Ok!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:11.050
Oneesama. Aren’t you a bit too kind to Ichigo?

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:12.690
I’m not.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:18.010
When you’ve fallen in love
I’ll give you my advice too.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.760
Heh, how mean.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:21.060
By the way...

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:23.070
What about the café?

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.240
Uhm, well...

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:30.570
Ahhh, how am I supposed to do all this!?

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.280
Smile, Ryou, Smile...

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.820
Smile!

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.620
Keiichirou, you little...!

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:38.050
Yes, I’ll be there in a second!

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:47.920
At first...

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.260
At first I was happy to watch you from far away.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:57.100
Just thinking and talking about you
with my friends made me happy.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:02.010
When we first got to talk. I still thought
it would never work out.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:05.440
I was prepared to be rejected,

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.440
but you said OK.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:12.660
I was so happy, so happy, happy!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.250
Our first date..

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:17.400
Walking next to you...

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.630
and hearing your voice,

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.530
all these things made my heart beat so much faster.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:25.710
But...

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:26.300
now...

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.010
I wonder if I’ve become greedy.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:36.850
Ma-sa-ya.

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.860
Ma-sa-ya.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:38.590
Ma-sa-ya.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:39.570
What?

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.060
I don’t mean you...

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:49.580
She didn’t say “Masha”?
So I’m not the one she needs.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:50.820
I’m sooo sorry!

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.540
Taaa-daaaaaa~!

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.240
It’s time for Bu-Ling’s fortune telling!

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.450
Today’s client is Ichigo, who is not too happy!

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:04.910
So now I’ll do a love test to see how
you and Aoyama-oniisan match up.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.470
Th... that’s... Thank you...

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:09.470
Now, switch on!

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:13.590
What’ll be the result?! So thrilling...!

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:20.360
Oooh, you did it. 100%, that’s love!
Right, Ichigo-oneechan?

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.050
Thanks, Bu-Ling.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.100
But I have to leave early today.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:25.820
I’ll go now, ok?

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:30.020
Huh, where did Ichigo go?

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.330
Ahh. you’re wearing the reindeer costumes! So cool!

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.730
I’m afraid we are a bit too late.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:36.690
Why, oh why?

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.280
I went through all this pain because you said if we wore these clothes, it’d cheer her up!

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.660
Should we go out and follow her?

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.800
That would be too embarrassing!

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:43.800
Leave her alone.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.280
Oneesama?

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.710
Now it’s up to her.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.400
Ichigo!

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:05.560
It’s become cold, don’t you think?
At this rate, Christmas might be whi–

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.320
I’m sorry.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:11.190
I need to go straight home today.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:13.140
Yes, all ri–

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.750
I’m really sorry.

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:15.660
Ichigo!

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.650
It’s no good...

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:20.210
As I thought, I can’t face him.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:28.680
<i>“Tears for Christmas”...
The meaning of “tears” is...</i>

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.500
<i>up to the lovers who own this.</i>

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.790
<i>But if the feeling of love is true,</i>

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:38.220
<i>it will be changed into a shining tear.</i>

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:44.770
Aoyama-kun is... so great.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:48.190
He’s good at sports, he’s smart,

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.850
and he knows a lot about the environment.

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:54.690
He plans to work in that field in the
future and studies every day.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:56.620
I am...

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.910
I am nothing.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:03.290
nothing... nothing...

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.710
Aoyama-kun...

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:10.540
How am I good enough for you?

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.380
How can I be with you?

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.050
But I always want to be with you.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.300
That’s all I want.

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:31.440
<i>We should just do what we know
we have to, little by little.</i>

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:36.190
That’s right!

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:40.740
Aoyama-kun always looks at everything directly.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.570
I...

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:46.790
I will also face him directly.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:49.170
because...

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:51.580
I love him.

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.800
I really do.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.050
Huh?

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:06.760
<i>Sorry about yesterday!</i>

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:10.600
<i>I’ll be waiting at the time, and at
the place, we promised! Ichigo</i>

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:21.780
I came too early.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.120
Oh well, it’s ok.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.590
What a nice wind...

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.500
Here at Odaiba’s Big Sight,

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:36.250
they are now about to light up the world’s biggest Christmas tree.

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:39.790
Ah, sorry, could you adjust this microphone?

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.840
Yes, yes, that’s it.

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:43.090
Hey, what’s that?

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:44.210
Yes? What?

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.510
Over there, over there.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:48.550
Is that the right one?

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:50.050
Don’t ask me.

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:52.280
Anyway we won’t find out
unless we try.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:53.970
You said it.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:56.530
Ok, let’s get this party started!

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:01.730
An energy rising!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.410
It’s the aliens!

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:03.480
Where?

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:04.650
Tokyo Bay...

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.420
No, on the reclaimed ground. Odaiba!

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.110
Go call Ichigo!

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.740
The others will head out right away too.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.340
Wait, that’s...

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:13.780
Ichigo is already in Odaiba!

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.050
She’s approaching the aliens
at high speed.

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:16.050
What?

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.050
Faster, I need to hurry more.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:27.010
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:07.730
<i>Emergency stop signal!</i>

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:12.690
<i>This train will return to the previous station, and will wait for the light to change.</i>

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:13.550
Everyone, this is not CG!

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:16.930
There’s people floating in the air, destroying buildings...!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.570
Th... that is...

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:21.600
That’s... That’s a Mew Mew!

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.120
Tokyo Mew Mew has appeared!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:26.440
Hey, you guys doing whatever you want again?

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:27.580
I won’t forgive you!

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:32.540
Once again, for the Earth’s future
I’ll be of service! ~Nya!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.500
Ooh, you’re early, kitty!

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.870
I don’t like hasty girls too much.

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:40.710
Shut up! I’m busy today!

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.710
So let’s fight and get it over with already!

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:44.210
I don’t get it.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:47.140
Why do you always support the humans?

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.460
Give me a break!

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.690
Because you guys want to extinguish all of us!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.590
“Us”? You’ve got to be kidding!

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:55.600
What?

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.560
Stop pretending you don’t know!

00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:01.100
You’ve already come to be more like us than a human!

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.600
You can’t communicate your feelings to the humans.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:07.040
No matter how hard you work, the
humans call you a trouble-maker.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.360
How many more times do I have to tell you? Fight with us!

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.620
Stop fooling me!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.000
That doesn’t... matter to me!

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.710
I’ve already decided to fight against you!

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:20.290
There she goes!

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.340
Success!

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.040
Massive energy reading!

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.580
The energy is resonating with Mew Strawberry.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:26.890
Damn! That’s what they want!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.480
I will protect them!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:33.060
I’m NOT working to be praised!

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:41.430
Oh!

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.940
That’s a Mew Aqua, no doubt!

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:48.190
Well done, Quiche.
It’s just as we planned.

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:50.240
It’s true; I should congratulate you.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.880
What’s wrong, Quiche?

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.200
Ichigo...

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.620
Why won’t you understand it!?

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:02.210
Idiot! You were serious!?

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.890
We won’t lose!

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.320
There’s no way we’ll lose!

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.260
Ichigo,

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.680
my precious Ichigo.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:32.550
You are open-hearted, a crybaby...

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:35.930
but just having you around makes my
heart feel at ease, mysterious girl.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.060
Do you know...

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:42.190
how happy I am just being with you?

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:44.390
Next time:

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:48.070
“Miracle of the Holy Night:
No Secrets Anymore”

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:50.110
Ichigo,

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.530
I’ll... always...
